  "analysis": "The BPE tokenization is confirmed correct ("The" → token 464). The transformer forward pass produces garbage output with both numerical and alphabetical layer ordering. The top tokens are single characters (559-569) with nearly identical scores (~118), indicating the hidden state is not discriminative. I need to test whether the weight matrices are transposed (stored as [output, input] instead of [input, output]) and whether the checkpoint uses natural ordering (wte, wpe first) instead of alphabetical.",
  "plan": "Write a debug program that tests 4 combinations: alphabetical vs natural ordering, and normal vs transposed weight matrices. Check which combination produces coherent top-5 predictions for "The" (expected: " best", " most", " first", etc. or similar common continuations).",
